- op: discuss  # 3a39
  at: '2026-11-14T02:23:10Z'  # 3a39
  by: agent  # 3a39
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3a39
  clock: 6  # 3a39
  nonce: 3a39  # 3a39
  message: "DONE in PR #2179, commit fd4fb93223 (\"fix(discovery): a file git ignores and does not track is not analysed\"). Owner ruling 2026-11-13: option (a), P1. ADR-0004 gained point 9.\n\nTHE RULE. A file or directory is left out when its work tree's ignore rules match it AND HEAD does not hold it. Both halves are git's own answer (git check-ignore --no-index --stdin, one call per directory level, paths on stdin; git ls-tree -r HEAD). No list of names; the index is never read. A committed file is analysed whatever rule matches it; an untracked file no rule ignores is analysed.\n\nWHAT HAPPENS WITH NO VCS, AND THE OTHER CASES THE ITEM ASKED ABOUT (each has a test): no VCS, a VCS other than git, git missing or failing: nothing is excluded. No commits yet: the ignore rules decide alone. A subdirectory of a work tree: the rules above it apply. The analysed directory itself ignored: nothing excluded (the user named it). A nested work tree: asked of its own git. Installed dependency source: its own rules, so an ignored node_modules/ is analysed under --trace-deps.\n\nWHERE. discovery (FileIndex.build, is_excluded / find_files, walks_into); the sketch readers that find a file by name or glob past discovery (27 sites: root manifests, the README and its links, licence and build files, the Structure listing); the profile's framework detection; supply_chain's manifest walk. Disclosed on stderr, in the sketch Overview and in supply_chain_summary.vcs_ignored_skipped. No opt-in.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE.\n1. The secrets case, measured before and after on one synthetic repository (5 committed files, 248 ignored and untracked ones, each holding a unique fake token; survey plus 8 sketches at 2k, 8k, 32k and 128k, with and without source). Before (dev 8b33e522b9): 134 of the 248 had graph nodes; the content of 18 appeared in every no-source sketch and of 16, 73, 107 and 107 in the with-source sketches at 2k, 8k, 32k, 128k; 42 in survey.json. After: 0 nodes and 0 files' content in every output, with and without the embedding model. A sketch of that tree equals the sketch of a clean checkout of the same commit apart from the disclosure line, and the graph nodes are identical.\n2. Framework detection: an ignored, untracked package.json naming express used to put \"express\" in the profile (11 frameworks from 6 ignored manifests in one probe); 16 manifest locations are now tested both ways (ignored: no framework; committed past the same rule: the framework).\n3. THE FILED REPRO, re-run on this repository's working tree with the code that merged (the tested tree and the merged tree are the same git tree, ec52ba5e27) (`hypergumbo sketch . -t 8000`, fresh cache). Before: every sketch carried \"[packages/hypergumbo-core/slice.json]\" under Configuration, and 19 of the tree's 31 ignored-and-untracked files had graph nodes. After: \"slice.json\" occurs 0 times in the sketch; 0 graph nodes sit on an ignored-and-untracked file; the Overview and stderr say \"Not analysed, because git ignores them and does not track them: .ci/.smart-test.lock, .ci/.smart-test.lock.pid, .ci/mypy-gate.log, 31 more (ADR-0004).\" and supply_chain_summary.vcs_ignored_skipped reports paths: 34. packages/hypergumbo-core/slice.json, .env and AUTONOMOUS_MODE.txt are still ignored and untracked in the tree (git ls-files -o -i).\n4. Tests: packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_vcs_ignored_untracked.py, 66 cases. Mutation controls: 53, each turned a test red. The first run of 51 left 19 green (sketch readers an end-to-end sketch does not reach, and one cache rule); each got a direct test and the second run was 21 of 21 red.\n5. Full local suite: 33,250 passed, 100% coverage on changed files. CI: green on PR #2179.\n6. Cost of the query: 0.05 s on this repository (6,279 entries, 10 calls), 0.23 s on kubernetes, 0.79 s on gitlab.\n\nNOT COVERED, filed as WI-dinuj-milus-kinuv-morir-judot-tibal-fagug-dobih: five readers that derive a fact from a manifest or count names without asking the rule. None prints a file's content. Also not done: any VCS other than git (nothing is excluded there, and the output does not say that no VCS was asked).\n\nWHAT IT COSTS. Source a build generates and the repository ignores (*.pb.go, a generated client) is no longer analysed in a working tree that has built it; calls into it are unresolved there, as they already were in a clean checkout. The disclosure names such files. There is no flag to turn the rule off."  # 3a39
